<h2>OS X</h2>
<ul>
	<li><a href="#mac">What players support Ogg Vorbis in OS X?</a></li>
</ul>

<h2>General</h2>
<dl class='faq'>
	<dt id='what'>What is Ogg Vorbis?</dt>
	<dd>
		<p>
			Ogg Vorbis is an audio compression format similar to
			MP3, but better because:
		</p>
			<ul>
				<li>it has a higher sound quality/filesize ratio</li>
				<li>has a standardized, flexible comment header</li>
				<li>is free, open, and unpatented</li>
			</ul>
		<p>
			More information about Ogg Vorbis can be found at
			<a href="http://www.vorbis.com/">vorbis.com</a>.
		</p>   
	</dd>

	<dt id='format'>Why are these files in .ogg format instead of .mp3?</a></dt>
	<dd>
		<ul>
			<li>Ogg Vorbis files sound better at smaller sizes compared to MP3 files.</li>
			<li>
				MP3 carries patent-licensing restrictions that don't apply to
				Ogg Vorbis.
			</li>
		</ul>
	</dd>
	<dt id='support'>What can I do if my player or operating system isn't supported?</a></dt>
	<dd>
		<p>
			Check with the maker of your software to make sure that it doesn't
			support Ogg Vorbis, because we may have missed many options in our
			FAQ. <strong>If your favorite player still does not support Ogg Vorbis,
			ask for it!</strong> The software community has been very supportive thus
			far, and user demand is what will drive adoption of Ogg Vorbis.
		</p>
	</dd>
	<dt id='encode'>I like Ogg Vorbis.  How can I make my own Ogg Vorbis files?</a></dt>
	<dd>
		<p>
			Standalone encoders for several operating systems are available on
			our <a href="http://www.vorbis.com/download.psp">encoder download page</a>.
			Here are our best bets:
		</p>
		<ul>
			<li>
				Using Windows? Try
				<a href='http://cdexos.sourceforge.net/'>CDex</a>.
			</li>
			<li>
				Using a Unixlike system? Try
				<a href='http://lly.org/~rcw/abcde/page/'><abbr title='A Better CD Encoder'>abcde</abbr></a>.
				If shell scripts scare you, try <a href='http://www.nostatic.org/grip/'>grip</a>.
			</li>
			<li>
				Using OS X? Try
				<a href='http://www.nouturn.com/oggdrop/'>Ogg Drop</a>.
			</li>
		</ul>
		</p>
			We also maintain a
			<a href="http://www.vorbis.com/software.psp">directory of software that supports Ogg Vorbis</a>.
		</p> 
	</dd>
</dl>
<h2>Windows</h2>
<dl class='faq'>
	<dt id='windows'>What players support Ogg Vorbis in Windows?</dt>
	<dd>
		<p>At least:</p>
		<ul>
			<li><a href='http://www.winamp.com/'>Winamp</a> (both versions 2 and 3)</li>
			<li><a href='http://foobar2000.hydrogenaudio.org/'>foobar2000</a></li>
			<li><a href='http://zinf.sourceforge.net/'>Zinf</a></li>
		</ul>
	</dd>
</dl>

<h2>Unix / Linux</h2>
<dl class='faq'>
	<dt id='unix'>What players support Ogg Vorbis in Unix?</dt>
	<dd>
		<p>At least:</p>
		<ul>
			<li><a href='http://xmms.org/'>XMMS</a></li>
			<li><a href='http://zinf.sourceforge.net/'>Zinf</a></li>
		</ul>
	</dd>
</dl>
<h2>OS X</h2>
<dl class='faq'>
	<dt id='mac'>I'm a Mac user.  How do I listen?</a></dt>
	<dd>
		<p>At least:</p>
		<ul>
			<li>
				<a href='http://xmms.org/'>XMMS</a>
				(through <a href='http://fink.sourceforge.net/'>Fink</a>)
			</li>
		</ul>
		<p>
			Additionally, there have been occasional reports of success with
			the expired <a href='http://www.macamplite.com/'>MacAmp Lite</a>
			with the provided registration codes, but
			<span title='Nathan Sharfi'>one of the webmasters here</span>
			has been unable to get it to accept the main registration code on the site.
		</p>
	</dd>
</dl>

<p style='font-size: smaller;'>updated March 12, 2003</p>
<%
self.write(box.finish())
%>

